# Final Cut, the part in bank 5 ($6060-$70F4): the code, the scroll text and its font. tools/endings_mkgame.py turns
# this file and the recording work/endings/fcw into src/endings/finalcut/fcmain.asm (src/endings/finalcut.json).

@equ $DB00 Pt3Init ; the PT3 player's init in bank 7 (aneS's src/music/pt3-player.asm, assembled at $DB00)
@equ $DB05 Pt3PlayEntry ; the PT3 player's frame
@equ $A66D AlienMagentaScreen ; the screens' labels (finalcut-screens.ann)
@equ $C16D CaptionScreen
@equ $DC6D VictoryScreen

@module fcmain ; Final Cut: the sequence, its scroll text and font
@about The game wins (aneG's GameWon): it copies the packed Final Cut block from bank 6 to $6060, and the HRUM depacker in front of it unpacks this image over $6060-$F76C and jumps to FinalCut. FinalCut copies Bank7Block (the green alien screen, the PT3 player and X-Man's tune REM) to bank 7 at $C000, starts the tune from an interrupt of its own (mode 2: the table at $5B00 filled with $60, the handler FcInterrupt at $6060), shows the caption screen for $500 frames, then the magenta alien screen and the scroll.
@about The scroll: two screens take turns, the normal one (bank 5, the magenta alien) and the shadow one (bank 7, the green alien), both reached through the $C000 window. Each frame one of them is paged in, its left 16 bytes scrolled up a pixel line (FcScroll, through the line table built over Bank7Block) and given the next pixel row of the text at the bottom (FcDrawRow), while the other is shown; so the screen flips between green and magenta every frame. The text (ScrollText) is 8 characters a row in a 16 x 16 font (ScrollFont); at its 0 the bottom row is cleared and FcTextEnd flickers the two screens for 460 x 2 frames, then FcVictory fades to white and shows the Victory screen, and the program stops in FcEnd (the music plays on).
$6060 c FcInterrupt ; the interrupt: one frame of the tune
> Mode 2 vector $6060 (the table at $5B00 holds $60). Saves every register, pages bank 7 ($17), calls the player's frame (Pt3PlayEntry) and pages $10 (bank 0, the normal screen) back; the main loop pages again after its HALT.
$608C s FcSpare ; free space, zero
$61A8 c FinalCut ; Final Cut: the caption, the alien and the scroll
> Entered from the HRUM depacker (the game's GameWon) with interrupts off. Never returns.
$61A9 ; black: border and attributes
$61AC ; bank 7 at $C000
$61B1 ; the alien screen, the PT3 player and the tune to bank 7 ($3578 bytes)
$61BC ; start the tune
$61BF ; bank 0 back, the normal screen shown
$61C4 ; the vector table at $5B00: 257 bytes of $60, so the vector is $6060 (FcInterrupt)
$61D1 ; I = $5B, interrupt mode 2
$61D9 ; the caption screen
$61E4 ; for $500 frames (26.2 s at the Pentagon's 48.83 Hz)
$61E7 FcCaptionWait
$61ED ; black again
$61F5 ; the magenta alien screen (the green one is in bank 7 at $C000)
$6200 ; the line table over Bank7Block (copied already): for each of the 192 pixel lines of the $C000 window, its address and the next line's
$6208 FcLineTableLoop
$6215 FcScrollFrame ; a frame of the scroll
$6217 FcDrawPage ; the page to draw on: $17 (bank 7, the shadow screen) and $1D (bank 5, the normal screen) in turn (the operand)
$6221 ; scroll it and draw the next pixel row of the text
$6224 FcShowPage ; the screen to show: $10 (normal) and $18 (shadow) in turn (the operand), with bank 0
$6230 ; and bank 7 paged with it
@isub $61B1 LD HL,Bank7Block
@isub $61B4 LD DE,AlienGreenScreen
@isub $6200 LD HL,Bank7Block
@isub $6203 LD DE,$C000
$6238 c FcEnd ; the end: loop forever (the tune plays on from the interrupt)
$623A c FcScroll ; scroll the left half (16 bytes) of the screen at $C000 up a pixel line, and the text's next pixel row
> SP walks the line table (POP DE the line, POP HL the line below it; 16 LDI a line, 3 lines a pass, until BC = 192 x 16 runs out), then SP comes back. A counts the glyph's pixel rows (0-15) in the operand of FcRow; at row 0 the text pointer (FcTextPtr+1) moves on 8 characters. A 0 there is the text's end: the bottom attribute row of both screens' left half is cleared and FcTextEnd takes over (the return address is dropped there); else FcDrawRow draws the row.
$623A ; SP into FcScrollSp's operand
$6241 ; SP = the line table
$6244 FcScrollLoop
$62AD FcScrollSp ; the operand: SP as it was
$62B0 FcRow ; the glyph's pixel row, 0-15 (the operand)
$62BB ; a new row of text: the next 8 characters
$62C5 FcTextPtr ; the text row (the operand; it starts 8 before ScrollText, so the first row is ScrollText's)
$62C9 ; 0: the end of the text
$62CE ; clear the bottom attribute row's 16 cells of the normal screen
$62DB ; and of the shadow one (bank 7)
@isub $6241 LD SP,Bank7Block
@isub $62C5 LD HL,ScrollText-8
$62F2 b FcRewind ; 6 bytes no path reaches: LD HL,ScrollText : LD (FcTextPtr+1),HL, which would start the text again
$62F8 c FcDrawRow ; draw pixel row A of the 8 characters at HL into the bottom line of the $C000 window
> The row's 2 bytes of each glyph (ScrollFont + (code - $20) x 32 + row x 2) go to the 16 bytes of pixel line 191 ($D7E0 through the window), one LDI pair a character.
$62F8 ; pixel line 191 of the window
$62FC ; IXl = the row's offset in a glyph (2 bytes a row)
@isub $6308 LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
@isub $6323 LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
@isub $633E LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
@isub $6359 LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
@isub $6374 LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
@isub $638F LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
@isub $63AA LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
@isub $63C4 LD BC,ScrollFont-$20*32
$63D5 c FcNextLine ; DE = the screen address of the pixel line below DE
$63E4 c FcPage ; A to the paging port $7FFD (BC kept)
$63EC c FcTextEnd ; the text is done: flicker the two screens, then the Victory screen
> Drops FcScroll's return address (the POP AF of the row count), shows the shadow and the normal screen in turn for $1CC x 2 frames (18.4 s; the alien flickers between green and magenta), then FcVictory and FcEnd.
$63F0 FcFlickerLoop
$6407 c FcBlack ; black: the border and every attribute
> Waits for a frame first (EI, HALT).
$6419 c FcVictory ; clear the screen, fade it to white, then the Victory screen
> Clears pixels and attributes from $5AFF down to the ROM (as Dead End's ClearScreen), then FcFadeStep with the eight FcFadeColours (black to white, 2 frames each), then copies VictoryScreen to $4000.
$6420 FcClearLoop
$642A FcFadeLoop
$6440 c FcFadeStep ; every attribute and the border to the colour at HL, then 2 frames
$6454 b FcFadeColours 8 ; the fade's attributes: paper = ink = 0-7 (black .. white)
$645C b ScrollText 8 ; the scroll text: 167 rows of 8 characters, then 0
@res text/scroll.bin
$6995 b ScrollFont 8 ; the scroll font: 59 glyphs ($20-$5A), 16 x 16 pixels, 2 bytes a row
@res fonts/scroll.bin
